---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const repos = [
  {
    name: 'inkbridge',
    href: 'https://github.com/desyncc/inkbridge',
    status: 'public',
    what: 'Mirrors the tablet\u2019s notebooks into an Obsidian vault: exports pages, transcribes handwriting, and injects daily journal entries. The most usable thing to come out of this work.',
  },
  {
    name: 'viwoods-mcp',
    href: 'https://github.com/desyncc/viwoods-mcp',
    status: 'public',
    what: 'The same notebooks over MCP, so an agent can read them behind a folder allow/deny list.',
  },
  {
    name: 'paper-console',
    href: null,
    status: 'private, for now',
    what: 'A handwriting-to-assistant console with a small on-device daemon. It is the project that forced most of the findings here; publishing it needs a scrub pass first.',
  },
  {
    name: 'viwoods (the SDK)',
    href: null,
    status: 'private, for now',
    what: 'Builds, reads and pre-flights .note files, parses the app\u2019s database, and drives import/append/move/purge against a device. 170 offline tests, ~99% coverage, and a live check that fingerprints every row so it can prove it changed nothing else.',
  },
];
---

<Base title="Code" description="What is public, what is private, and why.">
  <h1>Code</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Some of this is usable today. Some of it is deliberately not published, either because it is
    entangled with a device I own or because publishing it would be a security decision I am not
    making.
  </p>

  <ul class="plain">
    {repos.map((r) => (
      <li>
        <span class="claim">{r.href ? <a href={r.href}>{r.name}</a> : r.name}</span>
        <span class="chip" style="margin-left:.5rem">{r.status}</span>
        <p style="margin:.3rem 0 0">{r.what}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2>Why the SDK is not public yet</h2>
  <p>
    It is the piece I am proudest of and the piece with the highest bar: it writes into a device
    database, so its safety rules matter more than its features. The rules it enforces are taken
    from the app itself — the exact predicate the app uses for "this notebook has been to the
    cloud", the app's own quiescence signal before a snapshot, one import at a time because the
    importer deletes its own temp files. Before that ships, it needs its tests and its guards
    published together, not just the happy path.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you want to poke at the format, <a href="/posts/note-format/">the post</a> documents the
    container, the tables and the gates. That is the part that is worth reading first anyway.
  </p>
</Base>
